Z||000000||pollock||07-21-2000||05:05 PM||||Who makes the best repop GT sail panel?<P>Fiero Shop in N. CA.: $90<P>Fiero Heaven in AZ:  $99, available in smoked. <P>I would prefer the smoked, but am most interested in a quality part.||||reg||5
Z||000001||tgowens||07-21-2000||06:00 PM||||right now George at the Fiero Shop is out of them -- get in touch with 007Doug on here - he sells them too........<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/MY_SIGNATURE.gif">               <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||rockcrawl||07-22-2000||10:08 PM||||Hi,<BR> My '86 GT has repro quarter windows. I don't know who made them, but I can find out from the previous owner. I am not satisfied with them. The front edge is curved like the original, but the edges all the way around are not. They do not have the same exact contour of the originals, and they are wavy. The black printed or painted outline is coming off from what looks like expansion and contraction of the adhesive tape. It is also rubbed off from the inner panel at one spot, but this could be due to misaligned panels on the car. They are ok for an every day car, but if you want your car to be perfect, get GM windows. My '87 needed one, so I bought a NOS GM one for $160.<P>Jon<P>------------------<BR>'86 GT 3800<BR>'87 GT<BR>Rossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||13
Z||000003||Sillhouette.com||07-23-2000||10:59 AM||||Hi there!<P>I don't think that GM sells those windows anymore.  A guy here in Toronto bought the so called last set in 1993. He waited five months for it to be delivered from overseas somewhere.  <BR>All we are left with is the aftermarket products.  The one that you are describing is crap.  I got one of those on my car and can't wait to get rid of it.   <BR>Still searching for someone that can duplicat the original.<P>Later.||||reg||1
Z||000004||JohnnyK||07-23-2000||01:38 PM||||I found thsi place. I couldn't tell you if they are any good or not, but who knows?||||reg||1
Z||000005||JohnnyK||07-23-2000||01:39 PM||||(Mental note to include address)  <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Old Lar||07-23-2000||02:07 PM||||I ordered some GM GT quarter windows from my local Pontaic dealer in May. I'm not sure if they were new old stock or that these windows are being manufactured again.  The Parts manager said the order went through with no problem and I had them within a week.  They were costly devils at $200+ list a side.  Driver's side more expensive.<P>Since I have both reproduction ones and stock ones,  I was thinking of bringing them to the FOCOA convention for show and tell. Just to see what the differences are in a side by side comparison. ||||reg||6
Z||000007||tgowens||07-23-2000||02:28 PM||||JohnnyK, Paul McKibben's sail panels are for notchback only - not GT. there are a few out there selling GT sail panels. It is my understanding that the reproductions are being revised so that they are more like the original (curvature, rounded edges, etc) and will be a better fit. I, too, have the first generation repros and they are quite different from the original but, we must remember, as parts for these cars become more and more difficult to find, we may very well find ourselves in a situation where we are either faced with using reproduction sail panels or having a hole in the side of our car - in other words......the repros look better than nothing. That, coupled with the fact that, if and when we can find an original, it generally will cost more than the price of an engine swap!<P>This is just MY 2-cents but I'm willing to use repros if that is all that is available.<P>Check with 007Doug on here -- I do know that he is soon to have an "improved" reproduction GT panel.......aand, he's a good guy to deal with too!<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/MY_SIGNATURE.gif">                <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A><p>[This message has been edited by tgowens (edited 07-23-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||rockcrawl||07-23-2000||06:58 PM||||The Fiero Store is selling new GM replacements for $175 and $185. Either GM is still producing them, or they bought up a bunch of NOS parts. I haven't called to see if they actually have them, but they are listed on the website. <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fierostore.com/</A> <P>I described my repro windows as being pretty bad, but I would buy another set for a daily driver, considering the cost difference. My Fieros don't have to win any trophies.<P>Jon<P>------------------<BR>'86 GT 3800<BR>'87 GT<BR>Rossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||6
Z||000009||Bruce||07-23-2000||07:22 PM||||I bought my GT windows from the Fiero Shop and I'm very satisfied with them. I had them installed at a body shop so the fit would be correct and lasting. Plus the fact that I'm not very handy.||||reg||1
Z||000010||pollock||07-24-2000||11:23 AM||||Thanks for the input.  Anybody seen the ones from Fiero Heaven?||||reg||1
Z||000011||tgowens||07-25-2000||01:00 AM||||pollock, to my knowledge, all of the repros are the same and I believe come from the same source regardless of who sells them. I just put a new set of repros on my car today and they look good, although they are not quite the same as the originals, these are made of acrylic rather than lexan. The lexan tends to crack under stress and from heat from the engine vents where the acrylic will not. In fact, I removed the passenger side window without breaking it at all (which means I have one of the repros I may sell) so I can attest to the difference in pliability between the original and the repro.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/MY_SIGNATURE.gif">               <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A>||||reg||1
